Mind that if you take a turn to wish for something, and maybe another
turn(s) to use that wished item (put on, apply, whatever), you may as
well spend a turn to write the scroll. Usually you have scrolls stashed
away, so there's another turn to take into account anyway. Wishing is
typically nothing for Real Emergencies! (Even if your wish is already
available from a charged wand of wishing or magic lamp.)

You're right that a prepared scroll is useful, but mostly to charge his
wands of death, which have not as many charges as he probably will need.
Wands of teleport shall have enough charges as well. Such a wand with a
single remaining charge is helpful (break it!) if you get surrounded by
summoned monsters. (Don't apply to the Riders, though!)

